```java
String confUmask = conf.get(UMASK_LABEL);
int oldUmask = conf.getInt(DEPRECATED_UMASK_LABEL, Integer.MIN_VALUE);
if (oldUmask != Integer.MIN_VALUE) { // Property was set with old key
```
Reason:
The continued support for the deprecated `dfs.umask` configuration key allows users to set umask values using an outdated method. This can lead to confusion, as the code checks for the old key and may use its value instead of guiding users to the new configuration key, resulting in potential misconfigurations.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
// Remove the handling of the deprecated key
if (oldUmask != Integer.MIN_VALUE) { // Property was set with old key
